<title>USA: Ford seen boosting qtly dividend to $0.43 - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Ford seen boosting qtly dividend to $0.43 - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ford management is expected to recommend the company's board boost its quarterly dividend by 12 percent to $0.43 per share, the Wall Street Journal said in Thursday's electronic edition.</p>
<p>According to individuals close to management, the newspaper said the Ford Chairman Alex Trotman would likely recommend a $0.045 increase to the $0.385 payout rate Ford has paid for the past three quarters.</p>
<p>The company was not immediately available to comment.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
